course: dictionary
lesson: 10382
title: Treeless land
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Treeless means with no trees, or almost no trees. The word is made of tree and -less, and -less means without. So a treeless place is a place without trees. «The Arctic is the frozen top of the world... surrounded by the cold treeless land called the tundra.» The clues are cold and frozen: those words tell you why trees cannot grow there.
explain: Geographers often use treeless to describe a whole landscape, not just one spot. «A treeless plain» is a flat, open land with no trees on it. «Bleak and treeless» means a place that looks empty, grey and cold. When you meet treeless, ask: what is the weather like here? Strong wind, little rain or cold are often the reason.
explain: Think of how the sentence would change without the word. «The tundra is the flat land around the Arctic Ocean» tells you the place is flat, but treeless adds that there is not a single tree to break up the view. Swap in your own meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: Treeless means with no trees, or almost no trees.
fact: Trees cannot grow in some places because of cold, little rain, strong wind, or because people have cut them down.
fact: Treeless landscapes include the Arctic tundra, deserts, grasslands, high mountains and some windswept islands.
fact: «Tundra» is the flat, treeless land around the Arctic Ocean, frozen and dark for months in winter.
fact: «Treeless» is an adjective: it describes a noun, such as a plain, a land or an island.
exercise: What does treeless mean? | Very wet and full of rivers | *With no trees, or almost no trees | Covered in deep snow all year | Full of tall, dark forests
exercise: In «The tundra is the flat, treeless land... frozen and dark for months in winter», which word tells you the land is very cold? | buzzing | flat | boggy | *frozen
exercise: Give one reason why trees do not grow in some lands. | Too many mosquitoes | *Cold, little rain, strong wind or people cutting them down | Trees only grow in towns | The land is too bright
test: In «a treeless plain», what would you see? | A steep mountain with thick forest | *A flat, open land with no trees on it | A river full of fish | A busy town with many parks
test: Which of these places could be treeless? | A city park full of oak trees | A thick rainforest | *A desert | A dense wood
exam: Which phrase best means the same as treeless? | *with almost no trees | with flowers everywhere | under the sea | with many tall trees
